    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nai\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nIncorrect `it` match in the presence of an arrow function operator.\r\n\r\nGiven the following svelte snippet:\r\n\r\n```svelte\r\n<x on:click={() => 1}>aaa</x>\r\n```\r\n\r\n`it` will match: ` 1}>aaa`, whereas the match should be `aaa`. The error is caused by the early `>` sign which is part of the arrow function operator `=>`.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev-4e59422",
