            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nTag textobject has obvious limitations in 'mini.ai' due to it using Lua pattern matching by default. The current implementation indeed recognizes tag only up to the first instance of `>`.  As you did in #672, this can be customized, but I am hesitant to increase complexity of this textobject even further.\r\n\r\nSpecifically for tags a more sustainable and robust approach would be to use tree-sitter parsing and textobjects based on queries from 'nvim-treesitter-textobject': create filetype config file in 'after/ftplugin/xxxxxx.lua' (replace `xxxxxx` with the name of 'filetype' option inside which you need this specific behavior; not sure which one is set when working with Svelte) and define `vim.b.miniai_config` buffer local variable there:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal spec_treesitter = require('mini.ai').gen_spec.treesitter\r\nvim.b.miniai_config = {\r\n  custom_textobjects = {\r\n    -- Replace tags for captures which cover tags in the target filetype\r\n    -- See 'nvim-treesitter-textobject' queries to know more\r\n    t = spec_treesitter({ a = '@function.outer', i = '@function.inner' }),\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt will be more accurate but won't work inside comments and strings, though.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
