            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> hesitant to increase complexity of this textobject even further\r\n\r\nFair enough. Thanks for pointing me in the right direction. For those that come later, here is how I fixed it:\r\n\r\n1. Create file `nvim/queries/svelte/textobjects.scm` with the following contents:\r\n\r\n   ```query\r\n   ; These are mostly taken from upstream html/textobjects.scm, but with\r\n   ; `s/function/tag`. This is because upstream captures tags as @function, whereas\r\n   ; in svelte tags and functions may co-exist at the same time. Therefore, we now\r\n   ; explicitly capture tags as @tag instead of @function.\r\n   ;\r\n   ; Also see:\r\n   ; https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/blob/master/queries/html/textobjects.scm\r\n   ; https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects/commit/189468b62133d44fb6220530c8aa96718d0e93d1\r\n\r\n   (element) @tag.outer\r\n\r\n   (element (start_tag) . (_) @tag.inner . (end_tag))\r\n\r\n   ((element (start_tag) . (_) @_start (_) @_end . (end_tag))\r\n   (#make-range! \"tag.inner\" @_start @_end))\r\n\r\n   (script_element) @tag.outer\r\n   (script_element (start_tag) . (_) @tag.inner . (end_tag))\r\n\r\n   (style_element) @tag.outer\r\n   (style_element (start_tag) . (_) @tag.inner . (end_tag))\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n1. Create file `nvim/ftplugin/svelte.lua` with the following contents:\r\n\r\n   ```lua\r\n   local spec_treesitter = require('mini.ai').gen_spec.treesitter\r\n   vim.b.miniai_config = {\r\n     custom_textobjects = {\r\n       t = spec_treesitter({ a = '@tag.outer', i = '@tag.inner' }), -- @tag.outer and @tag.inner are defined in svelte/textobjects.scm\r\n     },\r\n   }\r\n   ```",
            "created_at": "2024-01-30T17:14:38Z",
